From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] TEST: wifi: ath11k: default the extension descriptor path to off

The tso parameter is the one gate of every frame sent through MSDU
extension descriptors: ath11k_dp_tx_ext() returns -EAGAIN without it, for
the TCP batches and for the scatter-gather frames alike, and with it off
at load ath11k_dp_tx_tso_wanted() keeps NETIF_F_SG, TSO, TSO6 and the
frame list features off the encap netdevs. Default it to off, so an image
that carries the extension descriptor patches sends none until tso=1 is
set; the netdev features follow from the next module load.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -18,9 +18,9 @@
 /* TEST-ONLY switch for the A/B of the TCL segmentation against software
  * segmentation of the same batches; dropped before this is upstreamed.
  */
-static bool ath11k_tso = true;
+static bool ath11k_tso;
 module_param_named(tso, ath11k_tso, bool, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(tso, "Let the TCL segment TCP batches (default: on)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(tso, "Let the TCL segment TCP batches (default: off)");
 
 /* Whether the netdevs of this device offer TSO and scatter-gather: the choice
  * is made when they are created, so the switch turns the TCL segmentation off
